## Implementation

### Canonical agent policy
Add `PR Merge Authority` near checkpoint/auto-continue rules in `.opencode/agents/adv.md`.

Define:
- explicit merge grant trigger;
- session-scoped lifetime;
- identity tuple: changeId + repo + `change/<changeId>` head + resolved default base + requested end-state;
- immediate canonical command `gh pr merge <number> --repo <owner/repo> --squash --auto`;
- remediation order: fix → push → re-read identity/state → arm/re-arm → verify `autoMergeRequest.enabledAt` while OPEN → waiter;
- terminal `MERGED` proof;
- invalidators, including restart/compaction authority loss;
- Tier-B separation and no-delete behavior.

### Capability law
Extend `.adv/specs/advance-workflow/spec.json` with a narrow MUST requirement for active-session same-change merge authority and scenarios for immediate arming, remediation re-arm, and drift/restart/revocation invalidation. Explicitly deny restart-persistent authorization claims.

### Tests
Add focused parsed assertions in `plugin/src/adv-autonomy-quality-assets.test.ts`. Assert session scope, identity bounds, invalidators, Tier-B preservation, re-arm sequence, canonical flags, arm verification, MERGED proof, and deletion prohibition.

### Structural boundary
This change governs active-session orchestration behavior only. It does not create a persisted authorization record or guarded merge tool. If restart-persistent authority is desired later, that requires a separate typed runtime/state-machine change.

## Source of Truth
Advance owns ADV-specific orchestration behavior. Existing deploy-local sync propagates `.opencode/agents/adv.md` to installed global configuration. Generic global instructions retain universal Git safety only.
